<section class="prose-legal prose-legal-section">
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
        EggInc.tools is the front door to a suite of Egg, Inc. fan tools, and one sign-in works across
        all of them. This covers the hub and the shared identity service behind that sign-in. Only the
        identity data needed to recognise you and apply your role or perks is stored. There is no
        advertising, no third-party tracking, and no analytics, and payment data is never handled here.
        Each tool has its own privacy policy covering the data that tool stores.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="prose-legal prose-legal-section">
    <h2>What the hub stores</h2>
    <p>
        Nothing about you. The hub keeps no account records, no analytics, and no per-visitor logs
        beyond the transient request logs any web server writes.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="prose-legal prose-legal-section">
    <h2>Signing in</h2>
    <p>
        Sign-in runs through the shared identity service at
        <a href="@ToolCatalog.DefaultIdentityOrigin" target="_blank" rel="noopener">id.egginc.tools</a>.
        It sits between you, an OAuth provider you choose (Discord, Google, Microsoft, or GitHub) via a
        self-hosted Authentik instance at auth.egginc.tools, and the tool you are signing into. Your
        password is never seen or stored here; the provider and Authentik handle it entirely.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="prose-legal prose-legal-section">
    <h2>What the identity service stores</h2>
    <p>When you log in, a single account record is created or updated holding:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>An internal account id.</li>
        <li>Your Discord user id, username, and avatar, if you have linked Discord.</li>
        <li>The role assigned to your account (for example viewer, contributor, or admin) on whichever tool you are using.</li>
        <li>When the account was created and when you last logged in.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        If you link more than one provider to the same account, each linked provider's id and the
        username and avatar it reports are stored too, so you are recognised on any of them. Linking
        anything beyond the first provider you log in with is optional. A custom avatar uploaded through
        your profile (up to 2&nbsp;MB, PNG/JPEG/WebP) is stored keyed to your account id and served back
        by the identity service.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="prose-legal prose-legal-section">
    <h2>Single sign-on cookie</h2>
    <p>
        Logging in to any tool in the suite sets one shared session cookie, scoped to the parent
        egginc.tools domain, so you do not have to log in again on the others. That cookie is also how
        the header can show your name instead of a sign-in link. It holds a signed token containing your
        account id, role, and a session id; it does not carry your password or provider tokens. The Sign
        out link in the header clears it everywhere, and the session id is revoked server-side so a copy
        of an old cookie cannot be reused. If you revoke access from the OAuth provider's own settings,
        the provider notifies Authentik directly and your session on every tool ends the same way.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="prose-legal prose-legal-section">
    <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
    <p>
        The hub sets no cookies of its own, and only strictly-necessary storage is used across the
        suite. There are no advertising or tracking cookies, so there is no consent banner to click
        through.
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>eggidentity_session.</strong> The shared sign-in cookie described above. HttpOnly, scoped to egginc.tools, removed on logout or expiry.</li>
        <li><strong>eggidentity_idhint.</strong> A short-lived, HttpOnly cookie used only to support clean logout and account re-linking with the OAuth provider. Not used to identify you anywhere else.</li>
        <li><strong>Antiforgery token cookie.</strong> Present on admin pages only, protects form submissions against cross-site request forgery. Does not identify you.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="prose-legal prose-legal-section">
    <h2>Supporter sync (GitHub Sponsors)</h2>
    <p>
        If you link a GitHub account and sponsor the operator through GitHub Sponsors, your sponsorship
        status is checked against the GitHub API, or received instantly through a signed GitHub webhook,
        and whether you are currently a sponsor is stored along with when that was last checked. This
        grants a Discord role and the related supporter perks in the tools. No payment details are ever
        seen here; GitHub Sponsors handles all billing.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="prose-legal prose-legal-section">
    <h2>What the hub asks other services</h2>
    <p>
        To show the version each tool is running, the server asks the shared deploy agent on a timer.
        Those requests come from the server, not from your browser, and carry nothing about you.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="prose-legal prose-legal-section">
    <h2>Data retention</h2>
    <p>
        Account data is kept while your account is active. Expired or revoked sessions are cleared
        automatically. Deleting your account removes your linked identities and any stored avatar along
        with it.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="prose-legal prose-legal-section">
    <h2>Removing your data</h2>
    <p>To remove the data stored about you:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Revoke access from your Discord, Google, Microsoft, or GitHub account's authorized-apps settings to cut the connection at the provider.</li>
        <li>Clear cookies for egginc.tools sites to remove the local session.</li>
        <li>
            Contact the operator through the
            <a href="@ToolCatalog.GitHubUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub organization</a>
            or the project
            <a href="@ToolCatalog.DiscordUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Discord server</a>
            to request deletion of your stored account record.
        </li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="prose-legal prose-legal-section">
    <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>
        This policy may change as the suite changes. The date at the top is the last revision. The
        hosted instance is run by an individual, David Cole, not a company. Source is at
        <a href="@ToolCatalog.GitHubUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/EggIncTools</a>.
        See also the
        @if (OnOpenTerms.HasDelegate) {
